---
import { catalog } from "../lib/catalog.js";
import { formatVerified } from "../lib/format.js";

const verified = formatVerified(catalog.meta.verifiedAt);
---

<div class="notice">
  <p class="data-note-label">About this data</p>
  <p>
    These are rows in NHTSA's ratings list, under the brand string that list stores. The list does not say whether a tire is still sold, and it has no category field.
    Light-truck tires, deep-tread winter-type snow tires, and temporary spare tires are outside the UTQG rule, so a missing line is not a grade.
    Sorting these rows is an ordering of NHTSA's list, not a ranking of the best tire.
    Data last verified {verified} (UTC). <a href="/methodology/known-errors/">Known errors</a>. <a href="/methodology/#data-quality">Data-quality notes</a>.
  </p>
</div>
